<%= @document.member.name %>'s <%= @document.title %>

<%= document_verdict(@document) %>

<% if @resolved && @timeline %>
Expires:      <%= @document.expires_on.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %>
Start by:     <%= @document.start_by.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %>
Lead time:    <%= @timeline.required_lead_days %> days (<%= @timeline.processing_days %> processing, worst case)
Applying:     <%= @resolved.domestic? ? "in #{Renewaru::Countries.title(@document.issuing_country)}" : "from #{Renewaru::Countries.title(@resolved.context)}" %>

<% if (slowest = @resolved.slowest_prerequisite) -%>
FIRST THING TO DO
<%= slowest["item"] %> — allow about <%= slowest["obtain_lead_days"] %> days to obtain.
This has to be in hand before you can apply, which is why the start date is so
much earlier than the processing time alone suggests.

<% end -%>
<% unless @timeline.feasible? -%>
NOTE: this cannot be completed before it expires. Even starting on the first day
you are legally allowed to apply, it takes about <%= @timeline.shortfall_days %> days longer than the
time remaining. Plan around the gap rather than around the deadline.

<% end -%>
Full playbook and the complete document list:
<%= playbook_url_for(@document) %>
<% else -%>
Expires: <%= @document.expires_on.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %>

We have no renewal rule for this document yet, so this is an expiry reminder
rather than a start-by date. Check with the issuing authority for how long
renewal actually takes where you are.
<% end %>

Your deadlines: <%= dashboard_url %>

--
<% if @resolved&.draft? -%>
These figures are unverified — nobody has yet checked this rule against the
issuing authority. Confirm at <%= @resolved.authority_url %> before relying on them.
<% end -%>
Reference information, not legal advice.
